WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.910
After the 2008 financial crisis,

2
00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:06.910
many central banks cut their
interest rates close to zero.

3
00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.160
But economies were still weak.

4
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.560
And rates cannot go far below zero,

5
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.570
because people could
simply hold cash instead.

6
00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.980
The usual tool had run out.

7
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.400
So when interest rates can go no lower,

8
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.930
how can a central bank
still get people spending?

9
00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:25.420
In this mission, you'll
follow a chain of effects

10
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:29.120
from the central bank to
household and business spending.

11
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.310
Then you'll use a graph lab to see why

12
00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.510
the same policy can close
a slump or barely dent it.

13
00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.510
Your mission: find out
what central banks did when

14
00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.360
their main tool hit the floor.
